I think that the way to avoid the problem is to not allow the
enormous piles of stuff in the first place.  The number of
objects it is possible to put in a pile is not realistic.  If
you want to eliminate the crock have a routine that has
excess objects placed in a square spill over into an adjacent
one and make movement through squares with many objects slow.
Maybe assign volume to objects based on their encumberance
and limit it that way.  This would create a real purpose and
value for sacks and chests.  

